  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pacific NDC Hub - Phase 4</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="4">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Active</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GGGI has been an implementing partner of the Regional Pacific NDC Hub since 2018, supporting Phases I to III, with GIZ as the lead partner. Phase III concluded in September 2024, and Phase IV is being implemented from September 2024 to September 2027. The first phase of funding is secured until April 2026, with additional funding expected from July 2026 for a further 18 months. The LOA ends in June 2026. Under Phase IV, GGGI is implementing four country requests in Fiji and Vanuatu to support enhanced NDC ambition, sectoral planning, and investment readiness. These interventions focus on strengthening national climate strategies, developing bankable investment pipelines, and advancing low-emission and climate-resilient development pathways.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overarching objective of the Regional Pacific NDC Hub is to support the realization of a sustainable, low-carbon, and climate-resilient Pacific. The Hub supports Pacific Island Countries (PICs) in the effective implementation of their Nationally Determined Contributions (NDCs) under the Paris Agreement, taking into account their national circumstances. Through coordinated support and partnerships across its internal and external network, the Hub aims to achieve the following: Improve NDC planning, policy, strategy and legislation in PICs. Strengthen enabling environment for NDC implementation. Accelerate NDC action and project/program implementation in PICs. Enhance NDC measurement, reporting and verification and transparency of climate action.</narrative>
  </description>
